{"changes":[{"target":"M10","current_line":"Recover failed payments automatically with smart retries.","type":"replace","change":"For subscription and membership businesses, lead with churn, not retries: 'How much of your churn is members who never meant to leave? Send us one month of failed renewals and we'll show you which ones are recoverable with a retry or an updated card.' Keep smart retries as the how, not the headline.","evidence":["E1","E2","E3","E4","E19"],"why":"The deal started when the customer split board-reported churn into cancellations and failed cards, and it turned once Tobi showed which of their failed renewals usually come back, so the customer's frame is 'members who never meant to leave', not failed payments.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":"M6","current_line":"Proven ROI, backed by an independent economic impact study.","type":"replace","change":"For the finance approver (e.g. the controller who holds the contract), replace the study claim with proof from their own data: 'Their file, not our average.' Offer a session that shows the recoverable amount in their last month of failed renewals, alongside exit cost and contract term, before the contract goes out.","evidence":["E20","E21","E25","E26","E16"],"why":"The contract sat with the controller for two weeks until he asked for the spreadsheet built from the customer's own export, and it was signed four days after that session, while he had also asked about termination fees twice.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":"M3","current_line":"Online and in-store on one platform; the line between them has pretty much disappeared.","type":"drop","change":"Stop leading with the unified online and in-store line with buyers whose front desk runs inside third-party studio software, unless we can show our reader working live inside that software. Lead with online billing and recovery first.","evidence":["E23","E29","E30","E36"],"why":"The unified pitch was heard as 'is that the readers?', the customer then asked to see the reader inside their studio management software, we could not show it live, and the front desk stayed with the incumbent with no date for phase two.","strength":"Test this"},{"target":null,"current_line":null,"type":"add","change":"When the incumbent counters with a rate review and a front-desk terminal bundle, separate the problems: 'Recovering failed renewals is a revenue problem a terminal bundle doesn't address. You can move membership billing without touching your front-desk hardware.'","evidence":["E10","E14","E16"],"why":"The incumbent answered with a rate review and a terminal bundle on a longer contract, which made 'everything' about hardware and exit costs, yet the deal was won on online membership billing alone.","strength":"Test this"}],"no_change_reason":null}
